<title>CROATIA: Croatia opens airspace to international traffic.</title>
<headline>Croatia opens airspace to international traffic.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia has opened its southern airspace to unlimited international traffic after five years of war that ended with a peace deal in Bosnia and normalisation of relations with neighbouring Serbia.</p>
<p>State news agency Hina, quoting a statement issued by the Ministry of Traffic on Thursday, said: &quot;All air routes above the Adriatic sea under Croatian and Italian jurisdiction are open to domestic and international airliners as of September 2.&quot;</p>
<p>During the fighting in Croatia and Bosnia that followed the violent break-up of federal Yugoslavia in 1991, the Adriatic airspace was open only to domestic, NATO and United Nations flights. -- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
